## Why This Is Asked

Addresses real-world needs for analytics while protecting sensitive SAP data. Evaluates understanding of data masking, per-tenant access control, and end-to-end data lineage.

## Key Concepts

- SAP data export pipelines to data lakes
- Field-level masking for PII/financial data
- Deterministic masking to preserve join feasibility
- IAM SCPs and per-tenant roles for isolation
- Data lineage via Glue Data Catalog
- KMS encryption at rest; minimal IaC for keys/roles

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: deterministic mask preserving format
function maskForColumn(val){ 
  if (val===null) return null;
  const s = String(val);
  const masked = s.replace(/[0-9]/g,'0');
  return masked.length>0 ? masked : val;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotence and integrity after multiple masking runs?
- What strategies ensure masking policies stay in sync with SAP authorization changes?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical data protection across SAP on AWS with Snowflake analytics, balancing real-time access and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- SAP S/4HANA data ingestion and masking
- Field-level masking rules for PII
- Snowflake masking policies and data sharing
- AWS KMS key management and IAM governance
- Auditing, rollback, and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example masking function
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).+(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{3})/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking without leaking data in logs?
- How would you rotate keys and propagate policy changes across Snowflake without downtime?
